From 9a48c7a199c8ef5d9c7ba800e582851baae1b531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Benjamin=20Cabe=CC=81?= <benjamin@zephyrproject.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:26:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] tracing: ctf: record zbus events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Record the zbus hooks as CTF events 0x186 to 0x197. Channels, observers
and async listener work items are recorded by address, like kernel
objects, so a viewer can name them from the image's symbols: channels
and observers are iterable section entries named after the C identifier
that defined them. Timeouts are in microseconds and results are the
functions' return values, as for the kernel object events.

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Cabé <benjamin@zephyrproject.org>
Assisted-by: Claude:opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Cabé <benjamin@zephyrproject.org>
---
